# row-group-key-logical.rq (loop N, AXIOM) — the group KEY for one aggregation row confirmed
# over the LOGICAL table (a continuation chain), whose member rows may sit on several pages.
#
# PRECONDITION (task 4 carry-in (a), stated because it changed under the perf rewrite): every
# member column this query is meant to reach must carry a tab:inLogicalColumn edge (materialized
# by document._link_columns for every column that actually took part in a licensed continuation
# — see tab.ttl's tab:inLogicalColumn comment). A column with NO such edge — a graph that never
# went through _link_columns, e.g. a hand-built fixture — makes this query REFUSE (zero rows),
# where the query it replaced (the `tab:continuesColumn*` property-path form, git history
# cfedaf3) still matched via the path's own zero-length case (?mc = ?lcol needs no edge at all).
# That is an honest behaviour change, not a regression: refusing over a graph that never
# recorded the correspondence is §7-safe, and no compile-produced graph reaches this query
# without the edges (document._derive_document_row_groups only calls it inside a chain, where
# _link_columns always ran at least once and asserts the reflexive edge at the head). See
# tests/etkl/test_derivation_equiv.py's negative pin, and feed._logical_column's docstring for
# the one place the two readings DELIBERATELY diverge (this query refuses; the feed falls back).
#
# THE SAME LAW as row-group-key.rq, over a BIGGER HOLON. The key is still the unique distinct
# non-blank cellText in the LABEL COLUMN among the member rows (?agg tab:aggregates ?m), and
# uniqueness is still a query-local closed-world guard — a holon-scoped guard inside an open
# derivation (§8). What grows is the holon it closes over: the page-local table becomes the
# logical table the pagination cut, so a member on page 2 is read by the same rule as a member
# on page 0. No unique value -> zero rows -> NO group (honest refusal, §7).
#
# WHY IT CANNOT SIMPLY BIND ?lcol: each member table mints its OWN column nodes, so "the label
# column" is a DIFFERENT URI on every page of the chain. The correspondence is not guessed and
# not parsed out of the IRIs — it is the asserted tab:inLogicalColumn relation, the reflexive-
# transitive closure of the tab:continuesColumn edges the continuation law licensed pairwise
# (clauses (b)+(c): column-for-column in both directions = a bijection at equal index). ?lcol is
# bound to the HEAD table's column, and the relation's reflexive edge at the head is what lets
# the SAME pattern reach a head cell and a continuation cell.
#
# SHAPE (loop N review — the derivation-scaling playbook, spec 2026-07-20):
#   * UNIQUENESS IS AN AGGREGATION, not a pair self-join. `COUNT(DISTINCT STR(?vx)) = 1` over the
#     members' non-blank label-column values says exactly what the NOT EXISTS pair scan said —
#     no second distinct non-blank value exists — in one pass instead of one scan per candidate
#     cell. Zero non-blank values gives 0, which the filter refuses, matching the old query's
#     empty result. STR() because the old comparison was on lexical form.
#   * THE COLUMN CORRESPONDENCE IS PINNED FIRST, in its own subquery, so the tiny
#     column-to-column relation is materialized before it is joined against cells rather than
#     re-derived per cell. Measured on the stem's 94-member witness: 21 s (pair self-join +
#     tab:continuesColumn* path) -> 0.26 s. Equivalence was proved differentially, not argued —
#     see the loop-N task-3 report.
#
# ORDER BY ?pg ?y picks the author's FIRST writing of the key in READING order — page first,
# then the cell's tab:y0 within the page. y0 alone is page-local and would let a page-2 cell
# outrank a page-0 one. tab:onPage is REQUIRED, not OPTIONAL: this query runs only over a
# compiled document graph, where every tab:EntryCell carries its page; a cell without one would
# make the ordering arbitrary, and refusing is the safe direction (§7).
#
# Bindings: ?agg = the tab:DetectedAggregationRow URI; ?lcol = the HEAD table's label column.
# The aggregation row's own label text is never read (no language matching).
PREFIX tab: <https://w3id.org/iladub/tab#>
SELECT ?v ?cell WHERE {
  { SELECT ?agg ?lcol (COUNT(DISTINCT STR(?vx)) AS ?n) WHERE {
      { SELECT ?mcx ?lcol WHERE { ?mcx tab:inLogicalColumn ?lcol } }
      ?cx a tab:EntryCell ; tab:atColumn ?mcx ; tab:atRow ?mx ; tab:cellText ?vx .
      ?agg tab:aggregates ?mx .
      FILTER(STR(?vx) != "")
    } GROUP BY ?agg ?lcol }
  FILTER(?n = 1)
  { SELECT ?mc ?lcol WHERE { ?mc tab:inLogicalColumn ?lcol } }
  ?cell a tab:EntryCell ; tab:atColumn ?mc ; tab:atRow ?m ; tab:cellText ?v ;
        tab:onPage ?pg ; tab:hasBBox ?bb .
  ?agg tab:aggregates ?m .
  ?bb tab:y0 ?y .
  FILTER(STR(?v) != "")
}
ORDER BY ?pg ?y
LIMIT 1
